1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
When will truly general-purpose robots
enter our daily lives and homes?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Their biggest obstacle today is
limited ability to generalize.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,020
This is a new starting point.

4
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:16,640
Over the next decade, with AI booming
and global interest rising,

5
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:19,350
robots are evolving much faster.

6
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:23,500
Progress may outpace
even my own estimates.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,000
When you can bring a robot
into an unfamiliar place,

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,500
even your home,

9
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,750
and it can complete
about 80% of tasks,

10
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:35,500
that will be the tipping point
for the industry.

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,100
At the 2026
World Robot Conference,

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,500
Wang Xingxing showed a robot
with record-breaking sprint speed.

13
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:47,300
He described self-evolving
physical AI robots

14
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:52,175
that use advanced models
to program and run themselves.
